WEBVTT

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:40.624
Giant space robot, this is Captain Fry

00:00:40.857 --> 00:00:43.110
of the U.S.S. Planet Express ship.

00:00:43.173 --> 00:00:44.466
We come in peace.

00:00:44.569 --> 00:00:45.737
Tough luck!

00:00:57.499 --> 00:00:59.376
Well, we destroyed the toy spaceship.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.461
- Now what are we going to do?
- Hey, look!

00:01:01.545 --> 00:01:03.380
The keys to the real spaceship.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:04.673
Do you think we should?

00:01:04.756 --> 00:01:07.009
Yes, I do.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:14.725
Leela, have you seen
the keys to the spaceship?

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.727
I must have left them on board.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.021
Well... I mean, what!

00:01:19.146 --> 00:01:21.356
Relax, the ship's not going anywhere.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.816
I anchored it with

00:01:22.899 --> 00:01:24.735
the unbreakable diamond tether.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:27.863
Oh, no.

00:01:27.946 --> 00:01:29.489
This isn't good for Zoidberg.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.039
Yeah!

00:02:04.566 --> 00:02:07.277
Hey, Fry, I'm steering with my ass.

00:02:07.361 --> 00:02:09.279
That's the best thing I ever saw.

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:31.301
That was great!

00:02:31.385 --> 00:02:33.637
And no one suspects a thing.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.721
Whoa!

00:02:41.269 --> 00:02:44.481
And that's how we learned our lesson.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.817
You've gone too far this time.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.068
All three of you.

00:02:48.151 --> 00:02:49.152
What did I do?

00:02:49.236 --> 00:02:51.113
You left the keys in the ignition.

00:02:51.196 --> 00:02:52.864
I mean, look at those two.

00:02:52.948 --> 00:02:54.950
Wasn't it obvious what would happen?

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:56.076
Yeah, Leela.

00:02:56.159 --> 00:02:58.578
We're all very disappointed in you.

00:02:58.662 --> 00:03:00.956
I should fire you three right now.

00:03:01.039 --> 00:03:03.333
But I'm just not that cold-hearted.

00:03:05.085 --> 00:03:06.336
You're all fired.

00:03:08.839 --> 00:03:11.550
Goodbye, friends. I'll miss you.

00:03:12.884 --> 00:03:14.177
Good riddance to them.

00:03:14.261 --> 00:03:16.430
Now Zoidberg is the popular one.

00:03:16.513 --> 00:03:19.725
Yes, yes, let's all talk to Zoidberg.

00:03:19.808 --> 00:03:20.976
Hey, Dr. Zoidberg...

00:03:21.059 --> 00:03:23.437
So, Zoidberg... What's new?

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.439
Oh, you know...

00:03:26.273 --> 00:03:28.191
What are we supposed to do for money?

00:03:28.275 --> 00:03:30.986
All I've got is
my frequent Taffy eater's card...

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:32.195
My first mustache...

00:03:32.279 --> 00:03:34.072
This picture of
my old girlfriend Michelle

00:03:34.156 --> 00:03:36.742
and that ski instructor
she was just friends with.

00:03:36.825 --> 00:03:38.535
Pardon me, brother.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:41.413
Care to donate
to the anti-mugging you fund?

00:03:41.705 --> 00:03:43.415
- Ow!
- We don't need to beg, Bender.

00:03:43.498 --> 00:03:45.334
For God's sake, we're not veterans.

00:03:45.417 --> 00:03:46.793
Well, what do you suggest?

00:03:46.877 --> 00:03:50.213
A daring daylight robbery
of Fort Knox on elephant back?

00:03:50.297 --> 00:03:52.049
That's the dumbest thing I ever heard.

00:03:52.132 --> 00:03:53.967
No, we can get jobs.

00:03:54.051 --> 00:03:55.761
But we just had jobs.

00:03:55.844 --> 00:03:58.430
Fortunately, I still have
our old career chips.

00:03:58.513 --> 00:04:00.557
- Our what?
- Career chips.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:03.727
You remember, they assign you
the job you're best at.

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.064
I tried to give you one and you ran away?

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.191
It's how we met?

00:04:09.274 --> 00:04:10.525
And then what happened?

00:04:10.609 --> 00:04:12.194
Just give me your hand.

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:13.945
Ow!

00:04:14.196 --> 00:04:15.280
Baby.

00:04:15.447 --> 00:04:16.448
Ow!

00:04:18.784 --> 00:04:20.577
I'd like to reapply for my old job.

00:04:20.661 --> 00:04:23.580
Counseling defrostees
and assigning them careers.

00:04:23.664 --> 00:04:26.041
Oh, I was hoping you would come back.

00:04:26.124 --> 00:04:30.212
I even saved your poster of a chimp
expressing your distaste for Mondays.

00:04:30.295 --> 00:04:32.589
Monday monkey lives for the weekend, sir.

00:04:32.673 --> 00:04:36.134
Just put your hand under the scanner
so I can verify your career chip.

00:04:37.552 --> 00:04:39.513
Calcutta, we have a problem.

00:04:39.596 --> 00:04:40.764
Delivery boy?

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.224
I must have mixed up the chips.

00:04:42.307 --> 00:04:43.308
It's a simple...

00:04:43.392 --> 00:04:45.852
Oh, here's our cryogenic counselor.

00:04:45.936 --> 00:04:47.896
- Do you like Mondays?
- They're okay.

00:04:47.979 --> 00:04:50.023
Then we'll have to redecorate your office.

00:04:50.107 --> 00:04:51.817
How do you feel about it helping

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:54.403
to be crazy to work here
but not being necessary?

00:04:54.486 --> 00:04:57.114
Hey! Let's see what it says about me.

00:04:58.198 --> 00:04:59.533
Welcome aboard, sir.

00:05:01.284 --> 00:05:03.787
Remember, when the tube opens, say,

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:07.874
"Welcome to the world of tomorrow!"

00:05:07.958 --> 00:05:09.126
Hey, I was frozen.

00:05:09.209 --> 00:05:11.795
I think I know what people want to hear
when they first wake up.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.632
Bathroom's that way.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.461
While you're on the probulator,
what brings you to the future.

00:05:19.544 --> 00:05:21.213
Oh, well, I wanted to meet Shakespeare

00:05:21.296 --> 00:05:23.131
and I figured that time was cyclical.

00:05:23.215 --> 00:05:24.591
Nope, straight line.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:27.135
Ah! The probulator's done.

00:05:27.219 --> 00:05:28.595
Oh, that wasn't so bad.

00:05:28.679 --> 00:05:30.722
Oh, wait, it hasn't started yet.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:36.353
Okay, it's about to start.

00:05:42.943 --> 00:05:45.821
Welcome to the future, human slave.

00:05:48.573 --> 00:05:49.908
Ah, relax, chum.

00:05:49.992 --> 00:05:52.035
I'm not really a giant fly.

00:05:52.119 --> 00:05:54.955
I'm a horrible robot!

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.500
Kill all humans!

00:06:00.919 --> 00:06:02.087
Dear God!

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.588
He's having a heart attack!

00:06:05.549 --> 00:06:07.926
They'll probably find
a cure for that in the future.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:09.803
We have a cure for it now!

00:06:09.886 --> 00:06:12.264
Oh, good,
then you won't mind if I use this.

00:06:20.606 --> 00:06:22.524
Nothing like a power nap.

00:06:29.364 --> 00:06:32.534
Flies, flies and gorillas!

00:06:37.581 --> 00:06:39.458
Stay beautiful, dollface.

00:06:40.042 --> 00:06:44.087
Whew! That probulator sure
knows how to please a man.

00:06:44.171 --> 00:06:45.589
So, what's for lunch?

00:06:45.672 --> 00:06:47.591
I ordered a pizza.

00:06:47.674 --> 00:06:49.343
Pizza delivery for...

00:06:49.426 --> 00:06:50.969
I.C. Wiener.

00:06:51.053 --> 00:06:53.555
Yeah, very funny.

00:06:53.639 --> 00:06:55.515
Now cough up the $12.95.

00:06:55.599 --> 00:06:58.018
Sorry, but if it's not here
in half an hour, it's free.

00:06:58.101 --> 00:07:00.103
It's only been 23 minutes.

00:07:00.187 --> 00:07:02.272
Well, I've got 33 minutes.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.443
It's only been 23 minutes,
you dumb cannoli.

00:07:06.526 --> 00:07:09.321
You got a problem? We can take it outside.

00:07:09.404 --> 00:07:12.032
Okay, I'll fight the box.
I think I can take him.

00:07:12.115 --> 00:07:13.450
Fry, just pay me.

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:15.786
I still owe 30 bucks on this uniform.

00:07:15.869 --> 00:07:18.747
Thirty-five, you stupid meatball!

00:07:20.248 --> 00:07:22.000
Who should we unfreeze next?

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:23.794
No.

00:07:23.877 --> 00:07:25.087
No!

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.215
Oh, my God! It's Pauly Shore!

00:07:28.298 --> 00:07:29.549
All right!

00:07:30.884 --> 00:07:33.720
Mr. Shore, I loved you in Bio-Dome.

00:07:33.804 --> 00:07:35.847
You sure caused some trouble
in that bubble!

00:07:35.931 --> 00:07:39.268
Rest assured, if it rhymes,
I can cause trouble in it.

00:07:39.351 --> 00:07:40.811
Hey, now that you're in the future,

00:07:40.894 --> 00:07:43.146
you can go live in an actual bio-dome.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.815
An unattractive prospect.

00:07:44.898 --> 00:07:46.400
While researching for the role,

00:07:46.483 --> 00:07:49.611
I ran computer simulations
demonstrating incontrovertibly

00:07:49.695 --> 00:07:51.822
that the whole bio-enclosure concept

00:07:51.905 --> 00:07:53.365
is fundamentally flawed...

00:07:53.448 --> 00:07:56.743
Be it expressed via dome, sphere, cube,

00:07:56.827 --> 00:08:00.789
or even the stately tetrahedron... Buddy!

00:08:03.208 --> 00:08:04.459
Oh.

00:08:04.543 --> 00:08:06.545
So, how did you wind up getting frozen?

00:08:06.628 --> 00:08:08.922
Well, while filming Encino Man,

00:08:09.006 --> 00:08:12.301
my intellectual curiosity
"Re: Cryogenics" was peaked

00:08:12.384 --> 00:08:15.012
and I resolved to freeze the weasel.

00:08:15.095 --> 00:08:16.513
The weasel!

00:08:18.015 --> 00:08:19.683
Hey, listen, Skippy.

00:08:19.766 --> 00:08:21.685
I was supposed to be unfrozen in Hollywood

00:08:21.768 --> 00:08:24.730
for the thousandth anniversary
screening of Jury Duty 2.

00:08:24.813 --> 00:08:26.148
How come I'm not there?

00:08:26.231 --> 00:08:28.442
I woke you up early
so we could hang out and do stuff.

00:08:28.525 --> 00:08:29.651
Like what?

00:08:34.656 --> 00:08:35.949
I love this job.

00:08:36.033 --> 00:08:37.534
Me, too.

00:08:37.618 --> 00:08:38.869
Show time!

00:08:38.952 --> 00:08:41.955
I'll pretend to be dying of space plague.

00:08:43.248 --> 00:08:44.583
Boo?

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:47.628
Michelle!

00:08:47.711 --> 00:08:50.339
Oh, my God.

00:08:51.923 --> 00:08:54.134
Fry? Is it really you?

00:08:54.217 --> 00:08:56.386
I don't know. Is it really you?

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:59.306
What do you mean you don't know?
Are you you or not?

00:08:59.389 --> 00:09:00.474
Who wants to know?

00:09:00.557 --> 00:09:02.517
Oh, Fry, it is you!

00:09:11.068 --> 00:09:12.903
I don't get it, Michelle.

00:09:12.986 --> 00:09:14.988
The last time I saw you,
you were doing great.

00:09:15.072 --> 00:09:16.740
You had dumped me
and were on your way

00:09:16.823 --> 00:09:18.533
to getting your life back on track.

00:09:18.617 --> 00:09:19.910
Why'd you freeze yourself?

00:09:19.993 --> 00:09:21.745
Oh, Fry, after you left,

00:09:21.828 --> 00:09:23.705
things took a turn for the worse.

00:09:23.789 --> 00:09:24.998
I got married.

00:09:25.082 --> 00:09:26.500
I'm sorry.

00:09:27.417 --> 00:09:29.044
His name was Charles.

00:09:29.127 --> 00:09:31.171
He attended a law school so prestigious

00:09:31.254 --> 00:09:35.008
the basketball team was coached
by Ruth Bader Ginsburg.

00:09:37.886 --> 00:09:41.556
I put him through law school by working
as a dog walker for antisocial dogs.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:44.101
- Sorry.
- But soon after Charles graduated,

00:09:44.184 --> 00:09:46.478
our marriage ran into difficulties.

00:09:49.773 --> 00:09:51.024
Uh... Sorry.

00:09:51.108 --> 00:09:52.526
Desperately depressed,

00:09:52.609 --> 00:09:55.362
I turned to the one thing
that could lessen my pain...

00:09:55.445 --> 00:09:56.989
A carnival.

00:09:57.072 --> 00:09:59.032
Unfortunately, a corn dog bone

00:09:59.116 --> 00:10:01.618
got lodged in the control panel
of the spizzler

00:10:01.702 --> 00:10:04.079
and I had to ride it for eight hours.

00:10:04.162 --> 00:10:05.205
Sorry.

00:10:05.289 --> 00:10:07.833
But it did give me a chance to think.

00:10:07.958 --> 00:10:08.959
I'm sorry.

00:10:09.042 --> 00:10:11.837
And I remembered the last
time I was truly happy.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.255
When I was with you.

00:10:13.422 --> 00:10:16.591
Aww. So you froze yourself
to come look for me?

00:10:16.675 --> 00:10:18.760
No, I did it to get a fresh start.

00:10:18.844 --> 00:10:21.471
I didn't know what had happened to you.
No one did.

00:10:21.555 --> 00:10:23.598
The police were going to conduct a search

00:10:23.682 --> 00:10:26.435
but your parents felt
it was a waste of taxpayer money.

00:10:26.518 --> 00:10:28.562
That's the same reason
they kept me out of school.

00:10:28.645 --> 00:10:30.731
So, no one even cared that I was gone?

00:10:30.814 --> 00:10:32.065
Not really.

00:10:32.149 --> 00:10:34.026
Except for one person.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:37.988
Who was it?

00:10:41.283 --> 00:10:43.535
Everything is so different.

00:10:43.619 --> 00:10:46.038
Not everything.
There's still a roach problem.

00:10:55.005 --> 00:10:56.214
Ugh!

00:10:56.298 --> 00:10:59.968
Nowadays, people aren't interested in art
that's not tattooed on fat guys.

00:11:00.052 --> 00:11:02.054
I'm on loan from the Louvre.

00:11:09.561 --> 00:11:10.854
Owww!

00:11:14.524 --> 00:11:16.234
Please, Professor...

00:11:16.318 --> 00:11:18.946
Give us our jobs back.
We deserve another chance.

00:11:19.029 --> 00:11:21.657
Yeah. And if you won't
give me another chance,

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.825
perhaps you'd give one to...

00:11:23.909 --> 00:11:26.995
Og, gorilla emperor of Earth.

00:11:27.955 --> 00:11:30.791
Sorry, Og. But I've got a new crew.

00:11:30.874 --> 00:11:34.252
So, how was your delivery
to Fantasy Planet

00:11:34.336 --> 00:11:37.089
where everyone's fantasies come to life?

00:11:37.172 --> 00:11:38.757
- Great.
- Organized.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:40.425
For one beautiful night,

00:11:40.509 --> 00:11:43.428
I knew what it was to be a grandmother.

00:11:43.512 --> 00:11:45.722
Subjugated, yet honored.

00:11:45.806 --> 00:11:49.351
You see, Og,
everything's running smoothly.

00:11:49.434 --> 00:11:53.105
And with Fry fired,
I can finally leave my jigsaw puzzles out

00:11:53.188 --> 00:11:54.982
without him eating the pieces.

00:11:55.065 --> 00:11:56.358
Forget about Fry.

00:11:56.441 --> 00:11:58.944
You could hire us back
and he'd never have to know.

00:11:59.027 --> 00:12:00.696
- Hey, guys.
- Oh!

00:12:00.988 --> 00:12:02.114
Hey, Fry.

00:12:02.739 --> 00:12:06.076
So, as Leela was saying,
Fry can go shove a big, old... Ow!

00:12:06.326 --> 00:12:07.494
I'm glad you're all here.

00:12:07.577 --> 00:12:10.205
I want to introduce you
to my on-again, off-again girlfriend

00:12:10.289 --> 00:12:12.457
of the past thousand years, Michelle.

00:12:14.334 --> 00:12:16.003
Michelle, this is Leela.

00:12:16.086 --> 00:12:18.005
This is Bender.

00:12:18.088 --> 00:12:19.965
The Professor.

00:12:21.675 --> 00:12:23.677
Hermes and Amy.

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:25.012
Nice to meet you.

00:12:25.095 --> 00:12:26.972
And this is Dr. Zoidberg.

00:12:29.683 --> 00:12:31.560
Dating your ex, Fry?

00:12:31.643 --> 00:12:33.687
Have you lost all self-respect?

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:36.857
- All what?
- This can only end badly, Fry.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.233
Kids, a house...

00:12:38.317 --> 00:12:40.444
A home invasion by a former roommate.

00:12:40.527 --> 00:12:42.070
But things are different this time.

00:12:42.154 --> 00:12:44.197
Before, she was demanding and possessive.

00:12:44.281 --> 00:12:47.492
But now she wants me to do stuff
and stay with her all the time.

00:12:49.202 --> 00:12:52.331
There you go, dearies.

00:12:54.291 --> 00:12:56.335
It's a relief to meet you, Amy.

00:12:56.418 --> 00:12:58.253
I'm just having a hard time adjusting

00:12:58.337 --> 00:13:01.048
to all the strange stuff
here in the future.

00:13:01.131 --> 00:13:02.341
I'm from Mars.

00:13:02.549 --> 00:13:05.218
I feel so out of place here.

00:13:05.302 --> 00:13:08.305
I don't understand
why Fry fits in so well.

00:13:08.388 --> 00:13:10.849
Probably because he didn't
fit in back in your time.

00:13:10.932 --> 00:13:12.100
That's true.

00:13:12.184 --> 00:13:14.269
But I used to fit in really well.

00:13:14.353 --> 00:13:15.771
Then good luck, sister.

00:13:23.528 --> 00:13:25.447
Don't take this the wrong way, Fry,

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:27.574
but your friends are a bunch of freaks.

00:13:27.658 --> 00:13:28.909
Yeah. They're great, huh?

00:13:28.992 --> 00:13:30.619
I just don't belong here.

00:13:30.702 --> 00:13:31.870
I don't know anyone.

00:13:31.954 --> 00:13:35.540
I can't find a vanishing cream
that doesn't make me actually vanish.

00:13:35.624 --> 00:13:37.292
I don't even have a job.

00:13:37.376 --> 00:13:39.586
Oh, right.
I was supposed to assign you a job.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:41.838
Let me just get
your career chip installed.

00:13:41.922 --> 00:13:43.924
Hold out your palm.

00:13:44.007 --> 00:13:46.635
What are you scared of?
It's like getting your hand pierced.

00:13:46.718 --> 00:13:48.595
This world is horrible.

00:13:48.679 --> 00:13:50.180
Let's start over, Fry.

00:13:50.263 --> 00:13:52.724
We'll go someplace where
all we have is each other.

00:13:52.808 --> 00:13:54.059
Ooh! Romantic.

00:13:54.142 --> 00:13:55.811
I'll tell Bender to meet us there.

00:13:55.894 --> 00:13:57.396
It's not a there...

00:13:57.479 --> 00:13:58.981
It's a then.

00:13:59.314 --> 00:14:00.524
The future.

00:14:00.607 --> 00:14:03.777
Whoa, girl, I thought you were talking
about one of those motels

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.445
where the bed is shaped like stuff.

00:14:05.529 --> 00:14:06.738
I love you.

00:14:06.822 --> 00:14:08.282
Don't you love me?

00:14:08.365 --> 00:14:09.408
Well, sure.

00:14:09.491 --> 00:14:11.368
To the extent a man can love a woman.

00:14:11.451 --> 00:14:13.120
But this seems like a big step.

00:14:13.203 --> 00:14:15.247
Fry, why must you analyze everything

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.749
with your relentless logic?

00:14:17.833 --> 00:14:20.252
Nothing matters but our love.

00:14:20.544 --> 00:14:21.586
You're right.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:24.464
Let's do this now
and let's never regret it.

00:14:42.357 --> 00:14:44.526
Michelle, I don't regret this,

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.486
but I both rue and lament it.

00:14:51.283 --> 00:14:53.702
The year 4000 is severely disappointing.

00:14:53.785 --> 00:14:56.204
I miss the year 3000, when life was simple

00:14:56.288 --> 00:14:59.166
and brains flew through space
and everyone ate lasers.

00:14:59.249 --> 00:15:00.292
It's not that bad.

00:15:00.375 --> 00:15:03.170
Fate brought us together,
and now fate brought us here.

00:15:03.253 --> 00:15:04.880
No, you brought us here.

00:15:04.963 --> 00:15:06.214
Whine some more, Fry.

00:15:06.298 --> 00:15:08.634
I really find that attractive in a man.

00:15:08.717 --> 00:15:10.719
Now, come on, build us a shelter.

00:15:10.802 --> 00:15:13.013
All right. Fine. Everything else sucks.

00:15:13.096 --> 00:15:15.182
At least we can have a nice place to live.

00:15:19.478 --> 00:15:20.771
Whew! There.

00:15:20.854 --> 00:15:23.231
You expect me to live
in a tiny, little hole?

00:15:23.315 --> 00:15:25.651
It'd be deeper,
but I'm standing on a gopher.

00:15:35.577 --> 00:15:37.079
Oh! Look!

00:15:37.162 --> 00:15:39.373
- Some little kids.
- They'll save us.

00:15:41.541 --> 00:15:42.960
We're saved!

00:15:48.924 --> 00:15:51.677
I'm Butch, leader of this place.

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:55.097
I took your hole and you can't
do nothing about it.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:55.889
Okay.

00:15:55.987 --> 00:15:58.266
Mighty sir, we have nowhere to go.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:00.519
Could we please join your society?

00:16:00.602 --> 00:16:02.271
Well... All right.

00:16:02.354 --> 00:16:04.731
But no interfering with our grand works.

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:14.366
I tell ya, that Butch runs
a pretty good civilization.

00:16:14.449 --> 00:16:16.660
I think I'll enjoy serving under him.

00:16:16.743 --> 00:16:18.537
You know your problem, Fry?

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:20.080
You're not ambitious.

00:16:20.163 --> 00:16:21.748
You should be chief.

00:16:21.832 --> 00:16:23.417
What do I need? Ulcers?

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:24.793
But I want power.

00:16:24.876 --> 00:16:27.254
I'm tired of the
chief's girlfriend lording it over me

00:16:27.337 --> 00:16:28.922
with her fancy coyote hide.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.968
All right, all right.

00:16:33.051 --> 00:16:35.679
If it'll make you happy,
I'll overthrow society.

00:16:38.682 --> 00:16:41.935
On what grounds do you
challenge my authority?

00:16:42.019 --> 00:16:44.146
Well, I'm older than you.
I can beat you up.

00:16:44.229 --> 00:16:45.564
Yeah, I bet he could.

00:16:45.647 --> 00:16:47.024
He's got arm hair.

00:16:47.107 --> 00:16:51.111
All right, Grandpa,
there's only one way to settle this.

00:16:51.194 --> 00:16:52.529
Death-rolling!

00:16:56.408 --> 00:16:58.785
- What's death-rolling?
- It's like skateboarding.

00:16:58.869 --> 00:17:01.204
Except half the time, someone dies.

00:17:01.288 --> 00:17:03.707
Oh, so it's a little safer
than skateboarding.

00:17:09.421 --> 00:17:12.799
Last one holding the bandanna
is the new leader.

00:17:14.259 --> 00:17:17.095
My mother always said
you were a loser, Fry.

00:17:17.179 --> 00:17:19.681
Now get out there and prove her wrong.

00:17:19.765 --> 00:17:21.141
Beth said that?

00:18:11.275 --> 00:18:13.485
It's cool. Back off!

00:18:14.444 --> 00:18:16.947
My knee, I scraped it.

00:18:19.116 --> 00:18:21.118
Aww. Poor little guy.

00:18:21.201 --> 00:18:23.161
Let me just take a look at... Aha!

00:18:23.245 --> 00:18:25.205
I won! I'm the new chief!

00:18:25.289 --> 00:18:27.416
I'm the tallest and I weigh the most!

00:18:27.499 --> 00:18:29.209
Hand it over, you giant idiot.

00:18:32.713 --> 00:18:34.464
Hey, Butch, your mom's here.

00:18:34.548 --> 00:18:35.632
Aw, man.

00:18:35.716 --> 00:18:36.717
Come on, kids!

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:38.385
You're late for Hebrew school!

00:18:38.468 --> 00:18:39.970
I don't wanna go.

00:18:40.053 --> 00:18:42.931
Every Monday and Wednesday,
it's the same thing.

00:18:48.186 --> 00:18:51.815
I find this postapocalyptic
wasteland very confusing.

00:18:51.898 --> 00:18:53.567
Seriously, I'm weirded out.

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:55.694
That's because you're a loser.

00:18:55.777 --> 00:18:57.821
You were a loser in the year 2000,

00:18:57.904 --> 00:19:00.324
and you're a loser in the year 4000.

00:19:00.407 --> 00:19:03.076
Yeah, but in the year 3000 I had it all:

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:05.454
Several friends, a low-paying job,

00:19:05.537 --> 00:19:07.039
a bed in a robot's closet.

00:19:07.122 --> 00:19:08.749
I envied no man.

00:19:08.832 --> 00:19:10.542
But you wrecked everything.

00:19:10.626 --> 00:19:13.712
Quit standing up for yourself, Fry.

00:19:13.795 --> 00:19:16.256
When we get back to the hole,
we are going to have

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.842
a long, boring talk
about our relationship.

00:19:18.925 --> 00:19:21.094
Oh, yeah? Well, listen to this!

00:19:21.803 --> 00:19:23.180
I'm leaving you.

00:19:36.276 --> 00:19:38.111
There must be people somewhere.

00:20:06.765 --> 00:20:08.517
Yes! Footprints!

00:20:09.101 --> 00:20:10.560
And handprints?

00:20:14.106 --> 00:20:16.358
But... What's happening?

00:20:22.572 --> 00:20:23.573
Fry!

00:20:23.657 --> 00:20:25.200
Thank God we found you.

00:20:25.284 --> 00:20:28.370
Leela, what are you guys doing here
in the year 4000?

00:20:28.453 --> 00:20:29.871
It's not the year 4000.

00:20:29.955 --> 00:20:31.915
You were only frozen for two days.

00:20:31.999 --> 00:20:34.042
By the way, I broke your bed.

00:20:34.126 --> 00:20:36.044
You were in Pauly Shore's tube,

00:20:36.128 --> 00:20:39.172
they were delivering it
to his movie screening.

00:20:40.507 --> 00:20:43.385
When they noticed you weren't him,
they chucked you in a ditch.

00:20:43.468 --> 00:20:46.096
So you're saying these
aren't the decaying ruins

00:20:46.179 --> 00:20:49.224
- of New York in the year 4000?
- You wish.

00:20:49.308 --> 00:20:50.892
You're in Los Angeles.

00:20:50.976 --> 00:20:53.061
But there was this gang
of 10-year-olds with guns.

00:20:53.145 --> 00:20:55.063
Exactly. You're in L.A.

00:20:55.147 --> 00:20:57.608
But everyone is driving around
shooting at each other.

00:20:57.691 --> 00:20:58.692
That's L.A. for you.

00:20:58.775 --> 00:20:59.985
But the air is green,

00:21:00.068 --> 00:21:02.404
and there's no sign of
civilization whatsoever.

00:21:02.487 --> 00:21:05.073
He just won't stop
with the social commentary.

00:21:05.157 --> 00:21:06.742
And the people are all phonies.

00:21:06.825 --> 00:21:09.036
No one reads.
Everything has cilantro on it.

00:21:11.538 --> 00:21:12.956
Michelle, baby.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:15.125
It's not working out, Fry.

00:21:16.335 --> 00:21:19.796
'Tis better to have loved
and lost, n'est-ce pas?

00:21:24.426 --> 00:21:26.428
That's it. I've had it with women.

00:21:26.511 --> 00:21:29.264
From now on,
I'm concentrating on my career.

00:21:29.348 --> 00:21:30.724
Can I have my old job back?

00:21:30.807 --> 00:21:33.852
Why, I've forgotten why I even fired you.

00:21:33.936 --> 00:21:37.648
'Cause he destroyed your business,
your home and all your possessions.

00:21:37.731 --> 00:21:39.358
Oh, that's right.

00:21:39.441 --> 00:21:40.651
Get lost!